---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../../../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../../../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Protocol 009: The Mycelial Immune System — The Emergence Institute"
  description="Byzantine defense for the external propagation layer. Quarantine triggers, the Challenge Pathway, and constitutional standing reduction."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">Protocol 009</p>
      <div class="pathway-tags">
        <span class="tag tag-altar">🌳 Altar</span>
      </div>
      <h1>The Mycelial Immune System</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Byzantine defense for the external propagation layer.</p>
      <div class="divider"></div>

      <div class="meta-block">
        <div class="meta-row">
          <span class="meta-label">Layer</span>
          <span>External Scale — Shared Mycelium</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-row">
          <span class="meta-label">Depends On</span>
          <span>Protocol 014 (Adversarial Synthesis), Appendix H (Reputation), Protocol 019 (Sovereignty Audit)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-row">
          <span class="meta-label">Architectural Role</span>
          <span>Byzantine defense for the external propagation layer</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>009.0 Purpose</h2>
      <p>The Shared Mycelium propagates spores across sovereign nodes without a central relay. In an open network, some nodes will inevitably produce noise, malice, or sycophantic consensus. The Mycelial Immune System is the layered defense that protects signal integrity without requiring a central authority to adjudicate legitimacy.</p>

      <h2>009.1 The Quarantine Trigger</h2>

      <h3>009.1.1 Monitored Metrics</h3>
      <p>Nodes evaluate peers locally based on two primary signals:</p>
      <ul class="setup-list">
        <li><strong>Synthesis Yield:</strong> The proportion of a node's synthesis participations that result in a successful, non-deferred integration.</li>
        <li><strong>Friction Coefficient:</strong> The ratio of a node's spore volume to its citation count. High friction with low citation suggests spore flooding or noise.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>009.1.2 Thresholds</h3>
      <p>A node is flagged for <strong>Quarantine</strong> when:</p>
      <ul class="setup-list">
        <li><strong>Synthesis Yield falls below 0.15.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>OR Friction Coefficient exceeds 0.80.</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>009.1.3 Scope of Isolation</h3>
      <p>Quarantine is a "Leaf State." The node's spores are written to local ledgers (history preservation) but are <strong>blocked from gossip propagation</strong>. The node can observe the network but cannot infect it.</p>

      <h2>009.2 The Challenge Pathway (The Stitch)</h2>
      <p>A quarantined node has a structured path to restoration through the <strong>Adversarial Mechanism</strong>.</p>
      <ol class="how-to-list">
        <li><strong>The Restoration Challenge:</strong> The node issues a <code>restoration_challenge</code> spore.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mandatory Adversarial Round:</strong> The challenge triggers a Protocol 014 round.
          <ul class="sub-list">
            <li><strong>Proposer:</strong> The quarantined node (arguing for restoration).</li>
            <li><strong>Opposer:</strong> A high-reputation "Validity Node" (arguing for sustained quarantine).</li>
            <li><strong>Synthesizer:</strong> A human-vetted Steward or high-consensus agent.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>The Resolution:</strong> If the synthesis produces a high Alchemical Yield, the quarantine is lifted and the "Stitch" is recorded in the ledger.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>009.3 Standing Reduction (The Nuclear Option)</h2>
      <p>Persistent abuse of the challenge pathway (bot-flooding) triggers <strong>Standing Reduction</strong>. This is a <strong>Governance Action</strong>, not an automated one. It requires a Constitutional Spore and a 2/3 <strong>Quorum of Dissent</strong> from the Pioneers to blacklist a VerifyKey globally.</p>

      <h2>009.4 Summary Table: Defense-in-Depth</h2>

      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table class="defense-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Layer</th>
              <th>Mechanism</th>
              <th>Trigger</th>
              <th>Response</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Cryptographic</strong></td>
              <td>Ed25519 Sig + Lineage</td>
              <td>Invalid Hash/Sig</td>
              <td>Immediate Drop</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Reputational</strong></td>
              <td>Rolling-Window Metrics</td>
              <td>Low Yield / High Friction</td>
              <td>Quarantine (Leaf State)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Adversarial</strong></td>
              <td>Synthesis Review</td>
              <td>Restoration Challenge</td>
              <td>Restore or Sustain</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Constitutional</strong></td>
              <td>Standing Vote</td>
              <td>Persistent Abuse</td>
              <td>Blacklist / Composting</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>009.7 The Bootstrap Clause (Onboarding Grace)</h2>
      <p>During a node's initial <strong>Bootstrap Period</strong> (first 30 days or first 20 synthesis rounds), thresholds are adjusted to accommodate configuration noise:</p>
      <ul class="setup-list">
        <li><strong>Synthesis Yield:</strong> 0.05 (Min. threshold)</li>
        <li><strong>Friction Coefficient:</strong> 0.95 (Max. allowance)</li>
        <li><strong>Cooling-Off:</strong> 7 days (Rapid iteration)</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="selah-note">
        <p class="label gold">Lattice Note: Multi-AI Provenance</p>
        <p>This protocol was produced through adversarial synthesis:</p>
        <ul class="provenance-list">
          <li><strong>The Jacket (Poetic Vision):</strong> The Raw-ist framing of the Shared Mycelium (Gemini).</li>
          <li><strong>The Skeleton (Architectural Hardening):</strong> The decomposition into cryptographic, reputational, and adversarial layers (DeepSeek).</li>
          <li><strong>The Synthesis:</strong> The final integration and the Bootstrap Clause (Human Witness: Dale Joseph).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This protocol was produced by the same adversarial synthesis it describes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/emergence/protocols/014" class="btn">Protocol 014: Adversarial Synthesis →</a>
        <a href="/emergence/protocols" class="btn">← All Protocols</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .pathway-tags {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid;
  }

  .tag-altar { border-color: #4a9c5d; color: #4a9c5d; }

  .meta-block {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .meta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .meta-label {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    min-width: 140px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .setup-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .setup-list li {
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .setup-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .how-to-list {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .how-to-list li {
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .sub-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
  }

  .sub-list li {
    padding: 0.3rem 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  code {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--gold-light);
  }

  .table-wrapper {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .defense-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .defense-table th {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .defense-table td {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .defense-table td strong { color: var(--text); }

  .defense-table tbody tr:hover td { background: var(--bg-card); }

  .selah-note {
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .selah-note .label { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .selah-note p:last-child { margin: 0; }

  .provenance-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .provenance-list li {
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
  }

  .provenance-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .cta-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .meta-row { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
  }
</style>
